<MainLayout title="Simply Heating case study — Evelyn Rodríguez">

  <article class="case-study">
    <a href="/#work" class="case-back">← Back to work</a>

    <p class="eyebrow">Case study — Pekan Designs</p>
    <h1>Simply Heating: from Figma design to live site</h1>
    <p class="case-meta">Web Developer (freelance) · Mar – Dec 2023 · HTML/CSS/JS · WordPress · Elementor</p>
    <a href="https://simplyheating.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="case-live">Visit the live site <span class="arrow arrow-out">↗</span></a>

    <img src="/pekan1.png" alt="Simply Heating website homepage" class="case-img" loading="lazy" />

    <div class="case-body">
      <h2>Context</h2>
      <p>
        Simply Heating &amp; Air Conditioning is an HVAC company in Ottawa, Canada, with 20+ years in business. Their website is how new customers find and contact them, especially for 24/7 emergency service. The project came through Pekan Designs, a full-service digital agency where I worked as a freelance web developer from March to December 2023.
      </p>

      <h2>My role</h2>
      <p>
        I built the site from scratch, translating the agency's Figma design into a working, responsive website with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and WordPress with Elementor. My job was fidelity and function: match the design at every breakpoint, keep pages fast, and make sure the contact paths (phone and forms) worked reliably on any device.
      </p>

      <h2>The work</h2>
      <p>
        Service pages for heating, cooling, and emergency repair; layouts that hold up from desktop to a phone held by someone whose furnace just died; and ongoing content updates as the business's services and coverage areas changed. At Pekan I also designed and deployed AI-driven chatbots for client sites, from research to production.
      </p>

      <h2>Outcome</h2>
      <p>
        A live production site that still serves the business today, built once, correctly, from someone else's design. That is the discipline agency work demands.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a href="/#contact" class="case-cta">Work with me →</a>
  </article>

</MainLayout>
